  "id": "Compound::DB00356 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Chlorzoxazone exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp1a1 and Cyp1a2, both of which are involved in the regulation of Aromatase Activity. This suggests that Chlorzoxazone may influence the activity of Cyp2d6 through the indirect pathway of Aromatase Activity. Additionally, Chlorzoxazone binds to Cyp2e1, which is involved in Oxidoreductase Activity, a process that is also implicated in the participation of Cyp2d6. These findings collectively indicate that Chlorzoxazone may modulate Cyp2d6 through multiple pathways, primarily by affecting the activity of Cyp1a1 and Cyp1a2, which in turn influence Cyp2d6. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Chlorzoxazone and Cyp2d6, although the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores suggest that the relationship is robust, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct involvement of Cyp2d6 in these pathways.",
